  {"id":"01M6SDRE8BYSD0BGRGMRRC0Q0Z","instance":["01M6RBNRG7D2ZC5P6JEVK0SY5G"],"body":{"title":"Selection and layering as interface","opens":"Selecting text as a way to interactability, since words carry more than characters: a selection a reach into the field at a level, the argument of a program, a buffer-stream until an act commits it. Layers over one text by lifetime: perpetual versions and branches, drawn diffs and nearness, temporary markings, a range over perpetual state made temporary as a marking. Pure drawing as the instant interface.","restsOn":["ranges, not yet specced","streams, specced by the first session","whether pureness is the function's or the program's, asked and not answered"],"stands":"noted","from":[{"$ref":"01M6SDRE845JZ69YCFTP045PQW","$holds":false},{"$ref":"01M6SDRE8AR46QRP102EFCZQRE","$holds":false},{"$ref":"01M6SDRE8APTKA4BV8QCEY6J46","$holds":false}]}}
